Play on a public server, if you are not already.  That's my advice.
Why?

Because I started playing on NAO, and I stopped quitting.  I used to do
it too.  I used to have a promising character and I would quit and kill
it on purpose because of boredom or the idea that I wouldn't be able to
get what I need.

I used to do this when I played offline.  I'd even go into explore mode
so that the score wouldn't show up.

But on NAO you can't do that.  I've quit a few times online and I think
it looks bad to say so and so quit or escaped.  So now I play each
character.  Even if I randomly generate a character that I meant to
select myself.  I was going for Samurai, got a Barbarian, and that
Barbarian did pretty well.  Eventually he died due to lack of MC3, but
he did pretty well.

I know not everyone looks at those high score lists.  But I do, and
when I see those promising characters that I quit I wonder to myself,
"Could I have recovered from my mistake or found what I needed farther
down?"  The answer is I probably could've.

Another character I quit was a rogue who killed his own priest because
it was my first time using Stormbringer.  I could have recovered,
mollified, and re-donated.  So now that is what I try to do when I
play.  I haven't blown up any BoH lately, but if I do I will keep
playing.  And before, that is something that would cause me to quit.

My other piece of advice is one that is already offered in this thread:
Go down, not up, when you need something.  There is always the chance
of finding what you need downwards (especially at the castle or orcus
town), but the chances of finding it in an old level are not good at
all.



